   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Kinetic Text\n\nA thin variable-weight word where a pointer sweeps over the letters: the letter under it swells to black weight with an outline, and its neighbours follow at lesser weights.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A word should feel alive with a wave of weight running through its letters.\n- A variable font headline needs an animated emphasis that moves along the letters.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text is long: letters reflow as their weight changes.\n- You want the letters to move rather than change weight: use per-character-rise.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Nostalgia\"\n- font_size (number, 24-400): Font size, default 192\n- color (color): Colour, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- step (number, 0.08-1): Step, default 0.22\n- start (number, 0-3): Start, default 0.4\n\nSource: https://github.com/magicuidesign/magicui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Kinetic Text\n\n  A thin variable-weight word where a pointer sweeps over the letters: the letter under it swells to black weight with an outline, and its neighbours follow at lesser weights.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/magicuidesign/magicui/blob/166367b4e31a27f166fd6c2b71d7be290fe0c1bc/apps/www/registry/magicui/kinetic-text.tsx\n  Changes by usemosio/blocks: the source reacts to the hover pointer; this block moves a pointer left to right over the letters, with the source's 0.4 s transitions.\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) Magic UI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"kinetic-text\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"The word. Letters reflow as their weight changes, so keep it short.\", \"default\": \"Nostalgia\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 192, \"min\": 24, \"max\": 400, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Colour\", \"description\": \"Text and outline colour.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"step\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Step\", \"description\": \"Seconds the pointer rests on each letter.\", \"default\": 0.22, \"min\": 0.08, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.02, \"unit\": \"s\"},\n    {\"id\": \"start\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Start\", \"description\": \"Seconds before the pointer reaches the first letter.\", \"default\": 0.4, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.1, \"unit\": \"s\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Kinetic Text</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100..900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .knt-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .knt-line { display: flex; flex-wrap: nowrap; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif); font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.05em; font-optical-sizing: auto; }\n        .knt-letter { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; -webkit-text-stroke-style: solid; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"kinetic-text\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"knt-clip\" class=\"knt-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <h1 id=\"knt-line\" class=\"knt-line\"></h1>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            // Shrink an element's font until it fits a share of the frame width.\n            function fit(el, size, share) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * share);\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (max / el.scrollWidth));\n                el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            // A seeded random generator, so every seek draws the same thing.\n            function mulberry32(a) {\n              return function () {\n                a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0;\n                var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a);\n                t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t;\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : x > 1 ? 1 : x; }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            var TAG = \"knt\";\n            var bezN = 0;\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return CustomEase.create(TAG + \"-\" + bezN++, \"M0,0 C\" + x1 + \",\" + y1 + \" \" + x2 + \",\" + y2 + \" 1,1\");\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            function finish() {\n              var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n              if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"kinetic-text\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            var line = document.getElementById(\"knt-line\");\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"Nostalgia\");\n            var color = col(vars.color, \"#0a0a0a\");\n            var step = num(vars.step, 0.22, 0.08, 1);\n            var start = num(vars.start, 0.4, 0, 3);\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            line.style.color = color;\n            line.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            var letters = Array.from(text).map(function (ch, i) {\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              s.className = \"knt-letter\";\n              s.id = \"knt-letter-\" + i;\n              s.setAttribute(\"aria-hidden\", \"true\");\n              s.textContent = ch === \" \" ? \"\\u00A0\" : ch;\n              line.appendChild(s);\n              return s;\n            });\n            // Bold letters are wider than thin ones, so leave room for the swell.\n            var size = fit(line, num(vars.font_size, 192, 24, 400), 0.8);\n            var n = letters.length;\n            // Targets: weight, side padding (em) and outline strength for a letter at distance d\n            // from the hovered one (negative = before it). Source: hovered 900, next 600, the one\n            // after 400 (and the same before it); padding on the hovered letter and its two\n            // immediate neighbours; outline only on the hovered one.\n            function target(d) {\n              if (d === 0) return { w: 900, p: 1 / 12, s: 1 };\n              if (d === 1 || d === -1) return { w: 600, p: 1 / 12, s: 0 };\n              if (d === 2 || d === -2) return { w: 400, p: 0, s: 0 };\n              return { w: 300, p: 0, s: 0 };\n            }\n            // Hover schedule: pointer enters letter i at start + i * step, leaves after the last.\n            var events = [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) events.push({ t: start + i * step, hover: i });\n            events.push({ t: start + n * step, hover: -1 });\n            var ease = bez(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1); // CSS \"ease\", 0.4 s as in the source\n            var TR = 0.4;\n            // Per letter: a chain of transitions that each start from wherever the last one is.\n            var chains = letters.map(function (_, li) {\n              var segs = [];\n              var cur = { w: 300, p: 0, s: 0 };\n              events.forEach(function (ev) {\n                var tg = ev.hover < 0 ? { w: 300, p: 0, s: 0 } : target(li - ev.hover);\n                var prev = segs.length ? segs[segs.length - 1] : null;\n                var from = prev ? valueIn(prev, ev.t) : cur;\n                if (prev && prev.to.w === tg.w && prev.to.p === tg.p && prev.to.s === tg.s) return;\n                segs.push({ t: ev.t, from: from, to: tg });\n              });\n              return segs;\n            });\n            function valueIn(seg, t) {\n              var f = ease(Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (t - seg.t) / TR)));\n              return { w: seg.from.w + (seg.to.w - seg.from.w) * f, p: seg.from.p + (seg.to.p - seg.from.p) * f, s: seg.from.s + (seg.to.s - seg.from.s) * f };\n            }\n            var strokeBase = size * 125 / 6000;\n            var clock = { t: 0 };\n            function draw(t) {\n              letters.forEach(function (el, i) {\n                var segs = chains[i], v = { w: 300, p: 0, s: 0 };\n                for (var j = 0; j < segs.length; j++) if (segs[j].t <= t) v = valueIn(segs[j], t);\n                el.style.fontWeight = Math.round(v.w);\n                el.style.paddingInline = (v.p * size).toFixed(2) + \"px\";\n                el.style.webkitTextStrokeWidth = (strokeBase * (1 + v.s)).toFixed(3) + \"px\";\n                el.style.webkitTextStrokeColor = \"color-mix(in srgb, \" + color + \" \" + (v.s * 100).toFixed(1) + \"%, transparent)\";\n              });\n            }\n            tl.to(clock, { t: total, duration: total, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.t); } }, 0);\n            draw(0);\n\n            finish();\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "fd3907710fe005acb07ef2baf8d447855f460be5ddd36589b6f15c74e1b12321",
